  "goodToKnow": "Der Idealismus is idealism, both as an attitude (viel Idealismus mitbringen, often said of volunteers and carers) and as a philosophy. Der Deutsche Idealismus (around 1790–1840), with Fichte, Schelling and Hegel building on Kant, is one of the great movements of Western philosophy. Der Idealist is an idealist, and idealistisch idealistic. It has no plural."
